 "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: Are you representing this process in a diagram? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: Absolutely! I'm representing it by using sequence diagrams.\n</br> <span class=\"strong\">Employee: </span> Is it describing the architecture or the state of a system?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager: </span>No, sequence diagrams don't describe that. We're using them to describe how a system works over a period of time. They aren't static, but dynamic. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Employee: </span> Are they showing the sequence of method invocations?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: Exactly! But between objects over a period of time. They let us know how objects collaborate in the particular scenario I'm proposing. </br>"}, {"time": "36000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: What is the diagram showing? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: We have two objects within a scenario where someone wants to withdraw money from an ATM. Vertical dashed lines show that time runs from top to bottom. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: Are still objects indicating actions for a long time after the loop?  </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: Sure! They continue expressing actions that take  place for as long as necessary.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: So, the user inserts his card into object1-ATM, during the same period of time Object1-ATM needs to verify it with the bank to find the user's account. The bank finds it and returns a value to let the process continue. Object1-ATM receives a message and it shows it to the user, then, ATM allows him to withdraw his money."}, {"time": "83000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: What other aspects are you taking into account?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: Remember \u2018ifs' and \u2018loops' </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: Do they give logic to the scenario? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: Exactly! The logic of a scenario depends on them,  the selection by using \u2018ifs' and iteration \u2018loops'.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: Are they making the diagram simpler?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager</span>: No. They clutter sequence diagrams, because we need interaction frames for representing them in sequence diagrams."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}